# Task FEATURE-004-US-002-T02 — Test & verify: Storage abstraction

> **DaemonCore coding-agent prompt.** Work type: `feature` · Size: `S` · Priority: `P1` · Status: `todo`

## Where this fits
- **Epic EPIC-004 — Saved Models.** Allow users to save, load, clone, delete, version and export/import policy models as structured JSON behind a storage abstraction designed for future database migration.
- **Feature FEATURE-004 — Saved Models — implementation.**
- **Story FEATURE-004-US-002 — Storage abstraction.** _As an architect, I want a storage interface so JSON now can become a database later._

## Objective
Add automated tests and verify acceptance for: Storage abstraction.

## What to do
Write **deterministic automated tests** that cover each acceptance criterion of the parent story:
- Assert: ModelStore interface defined with a JSON-file implementation
- Assert: No caller depends on the concrete backend
- Assert: Interface supports list/get/save/delete
Use fixed, hand-computed numbers (see `tests/test_fiscal_model.py`). Avoid randomness, network calls and time-dependence.

## Acceptance criteria (Definition of Done)
- [ ] Automated tests cover the story's acceptance criteria
- [ ] Tests are deterministic and pass in CI
- [ ] New/updated tests pass and cover the above
- [ ] No regression in the existing `pytest` suite

## Dependencies
Complete these first: `FEATURE-004-US-002-T01`.

## Project conventions
- Target Python 3.13. Use British spelling in all user-facing text.
- Keep the pure model layer (`model/`) free of Streamlit; `app.py` is UI/render only.
- Pin any new runtime deps in `requirements.txt`; test-only deps in `requirements-dev.txt`.
- Write deterministic `pytest` tests; follow the style of `tests/test_fiscal_model.py`.
- Match the surrounding code style. Prefer small, coherent diffs over broad refactors.
- Update `README.md` / `docs/` whenever behaviour changes.

## Guardrails (EPIC-004)
- Persist models as versioned structured JSON behind a `ModelStore` interface (DB-swap ready).
- Record engine and scoring versions with each saved model.
- Save/load and export/import must round-trip with no data loss.

## Verification
- `python3 -m py_compile <changed .py files>`
- `python3 -m pytest -q` — all tests pass (add/extend tests for this change).

